<title>BRAZIL: Brazilian soybean and product market.</title>
<headline>Brazilian soybean and product market.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brokers reported the following Brazilian soybean and products basis levels.</p>
<p>(NB - no buyer T-Trade P-Premium D-Discount)</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH		PREV</p>
<p>Soybean (cents per bushel)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April	     10/8 D	 April		12/9 D</p>
<p> May		 10/8 D	 May		  12/9 D</p>
<p> July		 6/4 D	 July	     2 D/even</p>
<p> August	   20/25 P	 August	    10/15 P</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH	   PREV</p>
<p>Soymeal/Pellets (dollars per short tonne 48 pct profat)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April		8/4 D	 March	     1.5/1 D</p>
<p> May		12/10 D	 May		  11/8 D</p>
<p> July	     16/15 D	 July		16/10 D</p>
<p> August	     7/5 D	 August		7/3 D</p>
<p> SHIPMENT	   BASIS	 MONTH	   PREV</p>
<p>Soybean Oil (dollars per tonne, points per lb, crude, degummed)</p>
<p>Fob Paranagua</p>
<p> April	  130/100 D	 April	   130/115 D</p>
<p> May	    180/130 D	 May	     160/130 D</p>
<p> July	   190/130 D	 July	    175/130 D</p>
<p> August	 150/120 D	 August	  170/120 D</p>
